Theorem 4. Alternatively, one can ﬁnd a new value (r0) for set-
cover size such that r0=r
mlog( ). In this way, we can make sure
that the set size will not be more than r. However, the distance
from the optimal solution may become larger than what provided
in Theorem 4. Applying the greedy approximate set-cover reduces
